CRITICAL CONSISTENCY RULES - NEVER CHANGE THESE:

OpenAI Realtime API parameters MUST always be:
- model: "gpt-4o-realtime-preview" (exact string)
- temperature: 0.2 (exact number)
- seed: 12345 (exact number)
- voice: "alloy" (exact string)

System prompts MUST be stored in lib/prompts.ts constants file. Never hardcode prompts inline.

Tool descriptions MUST be detailed and in Turkish. Each tool description must explain: when to use, what parameters mean, expected behavior.

VAD configuration MUST be user-adjustable with these exact parameter names:
- threshold (0.1-1.0)
- minSpeechDuration (100-1000ms)
- maxSilenceDuration (500-3000ms)
- preSpeechPadding (50-500ms)
- postSpeechPadding (100-1000ms)

All constants MUST be defined in lib/constants.ts file:
- REALTIME_CONFIG object
- VAD_DEFAULTS object
- AUDIO_CONSTRAINTS object
- SESSION_TIMEOUTS object

Session management MUST use Redis with exact key patterns:
- session:{participantId}
- score:{participantId}
- leaderboard:global
- questions:current

Error messages MUST be consistent and stored in constants. Never hardcode error strings.

Component naming MUST follow: ModernComponentName.tsx pattern.

TypeScript interfaces MUST be defined in types/ directory with proper exports.

Audio processing MUST use MediaRecorder with exact config:
- mimeType: 'audio/webm;codecs=opus'
- sampleRate: 16000
- channelCount: 1

WebSocket events MUST follow exact naming: onConnectionStateChange, onDataChannelOpen, onEventReceived.

Never use any type. Always define proper interfaces with required/optional properties.

All async functions MUST have proper error handling with try-catch blocks.

State updates MUST be immutable using proper React patterns.

File structure MUST follow: components/, lib/, types/, app/api/ organization.
